# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build context exclusions for the Django image (docker/django/Dockerfile).
# Keep the context small and never ship secrets / local state into the image.
#
# NOTE: Docker matches these patterns against the path relative to the build
# context root, so a bare `.venv` only excludes the root `.venv`. Use `**/`
# to exclude nested paths (e.g. `backend/.venv`, `backend/**/__pycache__`).
# Shipping a host `.venv` is actively harmful: `uv sync` would reuse it and the
# image would contain dangling interpreter symlinks pointing at the host.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Version control
.git
.gitignore

# Virtualenvs & Python caches (any depth)
**/.venv
**/venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/*.egg-info
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.mypy_cache

# Coverage / test artifacts (any depth)
**/.coverage
**/coverage.xml
**/htmlcov

# Environment & secrets
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Local persistent data, databases & generated assets
data/
**/*.sqlite3
**/*.sqlite3-journal
backend/staticfiles/
backend/media/

# Design / planning docs (not needed in the image)
terv.md
docs/

# Repo tooling / metadata
.github
.opencode

# IDE / OS
.idea
.vscode
*.swp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
